  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "4.10.0: Base character stats (GetClassBaseStatsAsync, GetRaceBaseStatsAsync, GetBaseManaAsync, GetCombatRatingsAsync). 4.9.0: Added SimcItem.Slot; fixed RaceId for Dracthyr, Earthen and Haranir. 4.8.1: Fixed the documented default branch name (midnight). 4.8.0: Item enchants (SimcItem.Enchant, SimcItemOptions.EnchantId); gems and enchants scale to the player level (SimcItemOptions.PlayerLevel). 4.7.0: Catalysed items use their redirected_base_stats item's base stats (RedirectedBaseStatsItemId); fixed stamina on Midnight items, gems with two stats and crafted item stats. 4.6.0: Fixed item levels for Midnight items (item scaling config, crafting quality and squish bonuses) and squished item levels for older items; added ContentTuningId. 4.5.0: Spell effect ChainTargets and ChainMultiplier; documented Delta. 4.4.0: Player spell effect ScaledValue and PointsPerLevel; fixed scale budget for scaling classes -9/-10 and spells with a max scaling level. 4.3.0: Talent rank values (SimcSpellEffect.RankOperation/RankValues); fixed talent data not being parsed and a stack overflow generating player spells with looping trigger spells. 4.2.0: Label-based spell relationships, plus SimcSpell.Labels and SimcSpellEffect.MiscValue1/MiscValue2. AffectedBySpellIds/AffectedSpellIds may now contain more spells. 4.1.1: GetAvailableTalentsAsync added to ISimcGenerationService, XML documentation included, README fixes. 4.1.0: Spell relationships (SimcSpell.AffectedBySpellIds, SimcSpellEffect.AffectedSpellIds). 4.0.0 (breaking): requires .NET 10 (net9.0 dropped) and Microsoft.Extensions.*.Abstractions 10.x. No public API was removed. Full notes: https://github.com/MechanicalPriest/SimcProfileParser/blob/master/CHANGELOG.md",
